                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A great game\r\n\r\nIts fun , especially when you get into the rhytm. Its hectic, \r\n\r\nThe music is great and I liked the variety in it.\r\n\r\nI liked how the gameplay flow, how you have to quickly reacts sometimes, and sometimes it goes more slow. Sometimes you just have to figure out witch notes you might want to skip to not get a double penalty. You lose score/bar if you miss a note, but you also lose if you let a note pass. Still I liked that you dont have to hit everyone to be able to beat it. Each stage feels good. And beside one of them witch I did on my first or second try, I needed more tries on the other stages. It might feel overwhelming, but you will start to memorise where notes or most of them fall. So is easier to be preperaed.\r\n\r\nThe story and characters is allright. \r\n\r\nI also liked the artstyle.\r\n\r\nMight be my first rhytm game finished, still recommended.",
